    "canonical_url": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/first-year/milestones/babinski-reflex-in-babies",
    "source_record_id": "raw_html_f8b9156ce7386d9a",
    "udare_article_path": "C:\\Users\\HP\\Documents\\LinkCraftor\\backend\\server\\data\\udare_store\\ws_whattoexpect_com\\articles\\first-year-milestones-babinski-reflex-in-babies_f8b9156c.html",
    "udare_article_sha256": "0c234eaa30606186ca388e0a9db15942980c4e471b750d9ea574025ce85cdfa8"
  },
  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/first-year/milestones/babinski-reflex-in-babies",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 27,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "What to Know About the Babinski Reflex",
        "text_sha256": "7c7850bdca3adf2ffc58133b83b06052a2008e396c5250decf9f78be50cd735f",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "babinski reflex, father stroking baby's foot",
        "text_sha256": "92085d974cf1a40bd899196340e181a18fb8afeefc216553903147eeb03ad3dd",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The Babinski reflex, also known as the plantar reflex, helps doctors test a baby’s neurological responses. Here’s everything you need to know.",
        "text_sha256": "0de3e42f1b5823341ffc7c0a5fa173b661c23cd170f0b3f122c31b8fb084da14",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "As adorable as they are, just-born babies do many odd things — at least from a new parent’s perspective. But all those strange twitches are signs that your baby’s nervous system is developing just as it should be.",
        "text_sha256": "b9cc92e04b8ff1f77ea30647d37a00df56d58dd564eeb9795a324729e887cd53",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "These newborn reflexes, sometimes spontaneous, sometimes in response to a touch or a loud noise, are your baby’s survival mechanisms. And while some may be obvious as to why they help babies thrive, others, like the Babinski reflex, are more subtle.",
        "text_sha256": "095476f5b12982d45d971ccce74b353e835cd5950376051f4afe12e8d7e6cff5",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What is the Babinski reflex?",
        "text_sha256": "f69efb9a03962165d69911b608fffa8ffc86645d8209d7ca5a9e19ff50589393",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The Babinksi reflex, also known as the plantar reflex, is an automatic response in your baby’s foot after it’s been stroked from heel to toe. The reflex is named after a French neurologist, who was the first to describe this response at the end of the 19th century.",
        "text_sha256": "452d987798ac019e4bc95028e13a7c688efe2ee68da2b1ade6edffbdfd3b81ad",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "So what is the Babinski reflex used for? Doctors test all the newborn reflexes at your baby’s first checkup to see how well his nervous system works. The Babinski reflex lets doctors know that the brain is sending signals to the spinal cord, which causes the big toe to flex upward as the other toes fan out when the bottom of the foot is touched.",
        "text_sha256": "1729ed3dbfec2256361ce5431097e077865c6ac4445de41f0af184ab2f645ba6",
        "word_count": 65
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "How long does the Babinski reflex last? Longer than the other newborn reflexes. It appears at birth and can disappear as early as 6 months or as late as 1 to 2 years old, after which the toes curl downward when the pediatrician strokes your toddler’s foot.",
        "text_sha256": "bd3e67e560e7ed299f5cf4774f60cb2dd9bc8a358809571873b422e615700912",
        "word_count": 47
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The Babinski reflex isn’t the same as the plantar grasp reflex (although Babinski is also known as the plantar reflex, which can be confusing). The plantar grasp reflex is just like the palmar grasp reflex, only with feet: Put your finger under your baby’s toes and they’ll curl over it. With the palmar grasp, those teeny-tiny fingers will grip yours when you touch your baby’s palm.",
        "text_sha256": "8939c0036e5fa98d261549a6d7754bf171d135661ade9015601fc8d131457d3c",
        "word_count": 66
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How do you test for the Babinski reflex in babies?",
        "text_sha256": "6e1bbca13acf2ca87acf3a622edb3719463f2427c0789401d6741a6c7c9bedb8",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here’s how to check the Babinski reflex: Take your finger and stroke your baby’s foot from heel to toe. As you do so, the big toe will extend upward while the other toes spread out. The foot will probably flex upward too.",
        "text_sha256": "a37977678c848dbb3328475ab3eeae1c0507b1c7ea051b59a8f8bcb746a0df91",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Where is the Babinski reflex tested? Well, the first check will happen at the hospital, though your baby’s pediatrician will look for it again no doubt during your baby's first well visits. Your health care provider will use a finger or a thin stick like a tongue depressor.",
        "text_sha256": "dacba591fd4e17120f208de485e6a2c5ab56310aff6556efb686943310fe18cf",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Is the Babinski reflex normal in babies?",
        "text_sha256": "47b69c8bf7ce1dba70ff377af486acdffdc32a36d03b20c06c5de99a1f1f7eac",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It is super normal in babies, and a sign that the brain and spinal cord (aka the central nervous system) are working together well. Again, in babies and toddlers, a normal Babinski reflex means the big toe flexes upwards while the other toes flare out once the foot is stroked from heel to toe.",
        "text_sha256": "e91d836d63d6be7f7795fd4eb9972a39f56fe529ac92dc82d19a7a1f2e7e7f4a",
        "word_count": 54
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "But if older children and adults have the same reflex, it could be a sign of something else going on that needs further testing. After age 2, your child’s toes should curl down once the foot is stroked. If they don’t, then the reflex, sometimes also called Babinski’s sign, could mean that something is wrong with the central nervous system.",
        "text_sha256": "26d2b4b3087e37825b786e0282682085f30fc9142d5968c19d4f1570d9d54d1f",
        "word_count": 60
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What does an abnormal Babinski reflex mean?",
        "text_sha256": "2cb432b7b961c8805ce3fcff4cea0b8da410c21c339488b0b27fbd92b8262be4",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Most healthy, full-term babies will show signs of the Babinski reflex when you run a finger along the sole of the foot. Even the majority of high-risk infants in the NICU — including premature babies and those with health conditions — have the Babinski reflex, according to researchers.",
        "text_sha256": "55fb08f7580e31083cb512d3f30a567fc5eb405125df8ece6f8a91b596d36c72",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In babies, an abnormal Babinski reflex would mean that your baby’s foot doesn’t respond at all to being stroked or responds weakly, or one foot responds differently than the other. An abnormal Babinski reflex could indicate that there’s something wrong with the signals the brain is sending to the spinal cord.",
        "text_sha256": "702610d8e8d54d953325bd08a3e23b917369d8fc68332cae37c082528e6bf472",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Children older than age 2 and adults who still have the Babinski reflex or have an abnormal one may have a problem with the brain and/or spinal cord, including:",
        "text_sha256": "f7aeadccae9bac52789ed40db8f6e72f142aa2dee337cb6b622e4b8b8373046c",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "A brain tumor or injury",
        "text_sha256": "98b91542bf5394f41a698d0364a06a8f1c5a8b43941582bcaee6b61f88bb0a1b",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "A stroke",
        "text_sha256": "8cd1fc3d116f2796e351d12d7e802a646f18d0c74e70a252e0cf94f43f135319",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Meningitis, an infection in the tissue surrounding the brain and spinal cord",
        "text_sha256": "c939a54189f8d4517d8e2332f54d009df7d0bdfca73c1f2fa143eb3db343f978",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Multiple sclerosis",
        "text_sha256": "142dd8216edaf74984de05adf3c685e9482c6a7e27d263b6d4b780cd830cfa2b",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "A spinal cord injury",
        "text_sha256": "94625cf25a484e20011f6c90b51e984471c57c1cd4ac9d107123e9aa9b119160",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If your child's Babinski reflex isn't normal, a doctor will order more tests to uncover whatever may be wrong.",
        "text_sha256": "a14a4c403173ed3f356075e50f0889e263e7eae15e72e4342de5d4bdc190a05a",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Even while your baby is lying still, he’s moving his whole body in small ways, including those newborn reflexes he's born with, that teach him about the world and his place in it. So while you're checking for the Babinski reflex, go ahead and savor your baby’s adorable little feet and tiny toes. Nuzzle them (they’ll never smell this good again!) or try a round of Little Piggy and other classic baby games . All that cuddling and attention will help your baby thrive — and bring you both closer.",
        "text_sha256": "824f29b403cae10d04326c534564d84be724e043348539f9c7e9b32b8f7f3aca",
        "word_count": 90
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 835,
    "heading_count": 5
  },
  "title": "Babinski Reflex In Babies: Normal vs. Abnormal, How to Test",
